<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black September</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1970">1970</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Black September was the armed conflict of September 1970 in which the Jordanian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">King Hussein</a> fought the Palestinian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> groups of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> Liberation Organization, which had built a state within a state in Jordan. A Syrian armoured incursion in support of the Palestinians was turned back. By July 1971 the fighters had been expelled, and the PLO moved its base to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-september.jpg" alt="Black September" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smoke_rises_above_Amman_during_Black_September,_1_October_1970.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
